<title>TURKEY: Turkish Turcas 1996 net profits soar.</title>
<headline>Turkish Turcas 1996 net profits soar.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)    1,248.25   vs   1,971.10</p>
<p>    Net profit		     2,533.98   vs   1,026.00</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     2,160.85   vs   1,566.26</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	   1,021.13   vs     211.81</p>
<p>    Exceptional expenses	   101.29   vs     174.88</p>
<p>    Interest paid		     65.06   vs	26.82</p>
<p>    Extraordinary income	 1,216.51   vs	54.92</p>
<p>    Total debts		    2,155.95   vs   1,264.23</p>
<p>    Equity			   8,508.86   vs   3,888.85</p>
<p>    Capital			  2,030.03   vs     520.52</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish petroleum products and lubricants marketer Turcas Petrolculuk is owned 82.16 percent by Tabas Petrolculuk A.S. which is owned 25 percent by American Conoco Inc</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
